    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23602" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-ŏboedĭo</span></b>  (or
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnŏbaudĭo</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 16</span></i>),
			īre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to disobey</i>, <i>be
				disobedient</i>, <i><span class="en">Ambros. Serm. Epiph.
			1</span></i>. — Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnŏboedĭens</span></b> ,
				entis, P. a., <i>disobedient</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Interp. Deut. 8,
				20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">ib. Tit. 1, 10</span></i>. — <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnŏboedĭenter</span></b> , <i>disobediently</i>, Aug. Civ. Dei, 14, 17.</div>
